  "aciklama": "SL-1 exploded during maintenance. The cause: prompt criticality from manual withdrawal of the central control rod, causing a steam explosion.\n\nFailure chain: Maintenance requires lifting a rod → Rod pulled too far → Prompt criticality → Steam explosion → Vessel jumps upward\n\nRelated episode: How Chernobyl Really Failed — https://youtu.be/Nk7vmybWY98\n\nFootage & sources:\n• Archival film: \"Sl-1-ineel61-9.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sl-1-ineel61-9.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Sl-1-ineel61-667.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sl-1-ineel61-667.jpg\n• Archival film: \"ALPR.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ALPR.jpg\n• Archival film: \"SL-1Burial.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SL-1Burial.jpg\n• Archival film: \"HD.6B.007 (10578937954).jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HD.6B.007_(10578937954).jpg\n• Archival film: \"HD.6B.006 (10579022233).jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HD.6B.006_(10579022233).jpg\n• Archival film: \"HD.6D.111 (10731009074).jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HD.6D.111_(10731009074).jpg\n\nTechnical references:\n• Wikipedia — SL-1 — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SL-1\n• NASA — sl1 sfcs (cited by Wikipedia) — http://pbma.nasa.gov/docs/public/pbma/general/sl1_sfcs.pdf\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Footage is real archival film or licensed stock; anything reconstructed is labelled on screen.\n\nFailure File · Episode 26 · A new engineering failure, reconstructed every day.\n\n#shorts #engineering #SL1 #nuclear #history",
